"""Build the offline source-matched tiger comparison player."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
from html import escape as e
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;D=R/'integrated';s=json.loads((D/'shot.json').read_text());checks=json.loads((D/'assembly-checks.json').read_text());fit=checks['mask_fit'];tr=checks['trace_fidelity']
css='*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f5f1e8;color:#171512;font:17px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1080px;margin:auto;padding:20px}a{color:inherit}h1{font-size:clamp(34px,7vw,62px);line-height:1.05;margin:24px 0 12px}nav,.tabs,.links{display:flex;gap:12px 22px;flex-wrap:wrap}.meta{font-size:14px;color:#625b50}.badge{display:inline-block;background:#ef9f3a;padding:5px 10px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700}.player{border:1px solid #d5caba;background:#fffdf7;border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden}video{display:block;width:100%;max-height:70vh;background:#fffdf7}button{font:inherit;border:1px solid #aaa18f;background:#fffdf7;color:#171512;border-radius:5px;padding:9px 14px;cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#171512;color:#fffdf7}.tabs{margin:14px 0}.keys{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}figure{margin:0;border:1px solid #d5caba;background:#fffdf7;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.pair img{width:100%;display:block}figcaption{padding:10px;font-size:13px}details{margin:24px 0}summary{cursor:pointer}footer{margin-top:30px;border-top:1px solid #d5caba;padding-top:16px;font-size:14px}.gap{border-left:4px solid #ef9f3a;padding:12px;background:#fffdf7}@media(max-width:600px){main{padding:14px}.keys{grid-template-columns:1fr}button{font-size:15px}}'
script="const v=document.querySelector('#film');for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('button[data-src]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{const t=v.currentTime,playing=!v.paused;for(const x of document.querySelectorAll('button[data-src]'))x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(x===b));v.pause();v.poster=b.dataset.poster;v.src=b.dataset.src;v.addEventListener('loadedmetadata',()=>{v.currentTime=Math.min(t,Math.max(0,v.duration-.001));if(playing)v.play().catch(()=>{})},{once:true});v.load()});"
cards=''.join(f'<figure><div class="pair"><a href="source-{k:02d}.jpg"><img loading="lazy" src="source-{k:02d}.jpg" alt="Source photograph for tiger key {k}"></a><a href="key-{k:02d}.png"><img loading="lazy" src="key-{k:02d}.png" alt="Full-scene tiger key {k}"></a></div><figcaption>Key {k} · source {s["frames"][f]["source_time"]:.3f} s · {e(s["xsheet"][f]["note"])}</figcaption></figure>'for k,f in enumerate(s['keys'],1))
reviews=' · '.join(f'<a href="{p.name}">Independent still review {p.stem.split("v")[-1]}</a>'for p in sorted(D.glob('review-v*.json')))
page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Tiger · moving drawing · Secondhand Motion</title><link rel="icon" href="../../../favicon.svg"><style>{css}</style><main><nav><a href="../../../index.html">Secondhand Motion</a><a href="../../moving-drawings.html">Moving drawings</a></nav><h1>The resting tiger turns.</h1><p class="meta">{s['frame_count']} frames · {s['fps']} fps · {len(s['keys'])} paired keys · {s['duration']:.3f} s</p><p><span class="badge">{e(s.get('review_badge','ASSEMBLED REVIEW COPY'))}</span></p><div class="player"><video id="film" controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="comparison-poster.jpg" src="comparison.mp4"></video></div><div class="tabs"><button data-src="comparison.mp4" data-poster="comparison-poster.jpg" aria-pressed="true">Source beside cartoon</button><button data-src="cartoon.mp4" data-poster="poster.png" aria-pressed="false">Cartoon</button><button data-src="source-excerpt.mp4" data-poster="source-01.jpg" aria-pressed="false">Source</button></div><p>{e(s['assembly_summary'])}</p><p class="gap">{e(s['review_note'])}</p><h2>Seven observed moments.</h2><p class="meta">Original footage at left; assembled drawing at right. Open either image at full size.</p><section class="keys">{cards}</section><details><summary>Drawing, source and checks</summary><p>Locked <a href="design.png">Quick, Draw! crouched tiger</a>, key {s['design']['key_id']}. Quick, Draw! contributors / Google Creative Lab, CC BY 4.0. The same 11 stroke identities and point counts are retained; the crouched striped body is held while head and eye anchors follow the source turn. No photographed tiger outline is substituted for the doodle.</p><p>Archive: <a href="{e(s['source']['page_url'])}">{e(s['source']['source_title'])}</a> ({e(s['source']['source_year'])}). Clip interval {s['source']['interval_seconds'][0]:.3f}–{s['source']['interval_seconds'][1]:.3f} s. Archive reports public domain; independent rights verification has not run.</p><p>Held background geometry: 100% unchanged. Character trace minimum recall {tr['min_recall']:.4f}, pieces retained {tr['min_parts_kept']:.1f}; required recall 0.98. Filled-rig/SAM fit mean {fit['mean']:.3f}, minimum {fit['min']:.3f}; required mean 0.65 and minimum 0.45. SAM model estimates are separate from this drawing-fit measurement. Recognition classifier and normal-speed motion approval have not run. Zero independently observed planted intervals does not pass the foot-slide gate.</p><p class="links"><a href="source-contact-sheet.jpg">Source contact sheet</a><a href="source.json">Source record</a><a href="shot.json">Editable timeline and strokes</a><a href="correspondence.json">Part correspondence</a><a href="assembly-checks.json">Measured checks</a><a href="traced.json">Character traces</a><a href="sam/provenance.json">SAM provenance</a><a href="compatibility.json">Source/doodle compatibility</a>{reviews}</p></details><footer><a href="cartoon.mp4" download>Download cartoon</a> · <a href="comparison.mp4" download>Download comparison</a><p>No training ran. These are review artifacts, not accepted training pairs.</p></footer></main><script>{script}</script></html>'''
(D/'index.html').write_text(page)
